<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Probus (emperor)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">232–282</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Marcus Aurelius Probus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-aurelius">Marcus Aurelius</a> Probus was Roman emperor from 276 to 282, a soldier from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sirmium">Sirmium</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a>. He drove Germanic invaders out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, secured the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> frontiers and settled large groups of barbarians, among them Bastarnae, inside the empire. He was killed by his own troops in 282.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/probus-emperor.jpg" alt="Probus (emperor)" width="320" height="488" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Probus_Musei_Capitolini_MC493.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
